<title>AUSTRALIA: AWB Australia wheat indicator prices - May 15.</title>
<headline>AWB Australia wheat indicator prices - May 15.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian Wheat Board international card prices for wheat exports for May 15.</p>
<p>In U.S. dollars per tonne, FOB eastern states.</p>
<p>		ASW	  AH     PH 13 PCT  PH 14 PCT</p>
<p>    May    210.00    213.50    214.00     220.50</p>
<p>    Jun    206.00    209.50    210.00     219.50</p>
<p>    Jul    203.00    206.50    207.00     218.50</p>
<p>    Aug    200.50    204.00    204.50     216.50</p>
<p>    Sept   200.50    204.00    204.50     216.50</p>
<p>    Oct    201.50    205.00    205.50     217.50</p>
<p>Note: ASW = Australian Standard White; AH = Australian Hard; PH = Australian Prime Hard; percentages = protein content.</p>
<p>Australian Wheat Board indicator prices for multi-grade contracts for 1997/98 crop wheat decreased A$1.00 per tonne.</p>
<p>	  Indicator Prices in A$ per tonne:</p>
<p>		  ASW 10 pct protein</p>
<p>    National FOB	184.00</p>
<p>Indicator prices on a delivered port basis:</p>
<p> Queensland			   South Australia</p>
<p>    Mackay	  159.50	    Port Adelaide	 161.00</p>
<p>    Gladstone     159.75	    Port Giles	    161.75</p>
<p>    Brisbane	157.50	    Wallaroo		159.50</p>
<p> New South Wales			Port Pirie	    156.50</p>
<p>    Newcastle     159.50	    Port Lincoln	  162.75</p>
<p>    Port Kembla   160.00	    Thevenard	     157.75</p>
<p> Victoria			     Western Australia</p>
<p>    Geelong	 159.00	     Esperance	    164.25</p>
<p>    Portland	160.00	     Albany		 165.25</p>
<p>					     Fremantle	    167.25</p>
<p>					     Geraldton	    165.25</p>
<p>NOTE: The indicator price represents the current state of the international wheat market. It is a cash contract fob price quoted on a delivered port basis, offered today by the AWB for wheat delivered during the 1997/98 harvest. The offer is valid until 4.30 p.m. Australian Eastern Standard Time (0630 GMT).  </p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
